# Implementation Plan: Chrome Extension for Smart-search

This plan outlines the creation of a Chrome extension that allows users to save URLs, images, and videos directly to their Smart-search knowledge base. It also includes the necessary integration with the React frontend to share the authentication token.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> To test the extension once it's built, you will need to:
> 1. Open Chrome and navigate to `chrome://extensions/`.
> 2. Enable **Developer mode** (toggle in the top right).
> 3. Click **Load unpacked** and select the `extension/` folder in your project directory.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Project Structure

I will create a new `extension/` directory at the root of the project with the following structure:
```text
extension/
├── manifest.json
├── popup.html
├── popup.js
├── background.js
├── content.js (optional/minimal)
└── icons/
    ├── icon16.png
    ├── icon48.png
    └── icon128.png
```

### 2. Chrome Extension Files

#### [NEW] [manifest.json](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/manifest.json)
- Define permissions: `tabs`, `storage`, `contextMenus`, and host permissions for the backend API.
- Register the `background.js` service worker.
- Define the `action` for the `popup.html`.

#### [NEW] [popup.html](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/popup.html)
- Create a clean, modern UI matching the app's aesthetic (dark mode, rounded corners).
- Add three buttons: **Save URL**, **Save Image**, **Save Video**.

#### [NEW] [popup.js](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/popup.js)
- Retrieve the current tab's URL and title.
- Fetch the authentication token from `chrome.storage.local`.
- Send a `POST` request to the backend API (`/api/items`) to save the content.

#### [NEW] [background.js](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/background.js)
- Create a right-click context menu with options for "Save Image" and "Save Video".
- Handle context menu clicks by sending requests to the backend.

### 3. Frontend Integration

#### [MODIFY] [useAuth.jsx](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/Frontend/src/features/auth/hook/useAuth.jsx)
- Update `handleLogin` to also save the JWT token to `chrome.storage.local` if the extension is detected. This allows the extension to "stay logged in" automatically.

